Input: {"question": "What is the medium of \"Green Pastures\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d00", "start": 0, "end": 183, "text": "The Green Pastures The Green Pastures is a play written in 1930 by Marc Connelly adapted from \"Ol' Man Adam an' His Chillun\" (1928), a collection of stories written by Roark Bradford."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d00", "start": 184, "end": 248, "text": "The play was the winner of the Pulitzer Prize for Drama in 1930."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d00", "start": 249, "end": 439, "text": "The play portrays episodes from the Old Testament as seen through the eyes of a young African-American child in the Depression-era South, who interprets \"The Bible\" in terms familiar to her."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d00", "start": 440, "end": 558, "text": "Following Bradford's lead, Connelly (a white man) set the biblical stories in New Orleans and in an all-black context."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d00", "start": 559, "end": 592, "text": "He diverged from Bradford's work,"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d01", "start": 0, "end": 232, "text": "Playing the ‘ What If ’ Game is the Wrong Thing to Do Remembering Who God is in Anxious Times The 7 Types of Love in the Bible The Extraordinary Gift of Letting Jesus Breathe on You What is the Church , and What is Your Part in It ?"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d01", "start": 233, "end": 269, "text": "What is God ’ s Rhema Word for You ?"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d01", "start": 270, "end": 487, "text": "5 Powerful Ways to Save People Left Outside the Gates The Positive Side of Loving Our Enemies The Real Danger of Spiritual Narcissism The 7 Elements of Nehemiah ’ s Great Prayer 3 Reasons Why Jesus Made Paul Blind The"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d02", "start": 0, "end": 124, "text": "into man’s attempt to find dignity and virtue within himself, that it invites introspection and a search for old dignities.”"}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d02", "start": 125, "end": 374, "text": "III The Novel The Green Pastures is not a novel utterly different from everything that Connelly had done before; The Deep Tangled Wildwood, The Wisdom Tooth, and The Wild Man of Borneo, for examples, are quite obviously searches for “old dignities.”"}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d02", "start": 375, "end": 452, "text": "What distinguishes The Green Pastures from these earlier novels is its scope."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d02", "start": 453, "end": 547, "text": "In this novel Connelly selected his materials, not from minor aspects of contemporary society."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d03", "start": 0, "end": 230, "text": "Playing the ‘ What If ’ Game is the Wrong Thing to Do Remembering Who God is in Anxious Times The 7 Types of Love in the Bible The Extraordinary Gift of Letting Jesus Breathe on You What is the Church, and What is Your Part in It?"}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d03", "start": 231, "end": 266, "text": "What is God ’ s Rhema Word for You?"}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d03", "start": 267, "end": 564, "text": "5 Powerful Ways to Save People Left Outside the Gates The Positive Side of Loving Our Enemies The Real Danger of Spiritual Narcissism The 7 Elements of Nehemiah ’ s Great Prayer 3 Reasons Why Jesus Made Paul Blind The \"Green Pastures\" is a novel that explores deep spiritual themes and narratives."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d04", "start": 0, "end": 147, "text": "The Green Pastures (film) The Green Pastures is a 1936 American film depicting stories from the Bible as visualized by African-American characters."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d04", "start": 148, "end": 254, "text": "It starred Rex Ingram (in several roles, including \"De Lawd\"), Oscar Polk, and Eddie \"Rochester\" Anderson."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d04", "start": 255, "end": 410, "text": "It was based on the 1928 novel \"Ol' Man Adam an' His Chillun\" by Roark Bradford and the 1930 Pulitzer Prize-winning play of the same name by Marc Connelly."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d04", "start": 411, "end": 603, "text": "The Green Pastures was one of only six feature films in the Hollywood Studio era to feature an all-African American cast, though elements of it were criticised by civil rights activists at the"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d05", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "Judith ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d05", "start": 9, "end": 89, "text": "Hollywood Be Thy Name : African American Religion in American Film , 1929-1949 ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d05", "start": 90, "end": 140, "text": "Berkeley : University of California Press , 2007 ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0131-629541a2de9a:d05", "start": 141, "end": 652, "text": "Column 1 Company About EBSCO Leadership Offices Careers Column 2 Commitments Open for Research Open Access Accessibility Artificial Intelligence ( AI ) Column 3 Values Carbon Neutrality Trust & Security Corporate Responsibility Our People & Community Column 4 Log In EBSCOhost EBSCONET EBSCOadmin EBSCOhost Collection Manager EBSCO Experience Manager Column 5 Social bar Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Inst